# ML Core layer for macOS Apple Silicon (Darwin arm64)
# Target-owned lockfile for deterministic pip-compile resolution.
#
# This file is Apple Silicon-specific so the repo can keep Intel-only
# compatibility caps isolated to the x86_64 lock while allowing the arm64
# baseline to carry Core ML support.
#
# Run `make compile-ml-darwin-arm64` in this directory to generate pinned ml-core-darwin-arm64.txt
#
# PLATFORM TARGETS:
#   - darwin-arm64-cpu    (macOS Apple Silicon, CPU fallback)
#   - darwin-arm64-mps    (macOS Apple Silicon, Metal)
#
# SECURITY NOTE:
# - Supported Apple Silicon lock rotations now anchor on torch==2.8.0 /
#   torchvision==0.23.0.
# - weights_only=True remains mandatory defense in depth for all checkpoint loads.
#
# APPLE SILICON POLICY:
# - DepthPro/Core ML integration is allowed only on Apple Silicon
# - CoreML tooling belongs in this lock so the Apple depth stack is explicit
# - Intel-only caps such as numpy<2 do not belong in this arm64 input
#
# See: requirements/README.md for layering rationale.

# --- PyTorch (Apple Silicon supported baseline) ---
torch==2.8.0  # Supported security baseline
torchvision==0.23.0  # Paired Apple Silicon baseline

